  "question": {
    "text": "The equation of the normal to the parabola, $x^2=8 y$ at $x=4$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "SAxzZ",
      "text": "\n$x+2 y=0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "dxv1l",
      "text": "\n$x+y=2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "f0jHf",
      "text": "\n$x-2 y=0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "eenjk",
      "text": "\n$x+y=6$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$x^2=8 y$\nWhen, $x=4$, then $y=2$\nNow $\\left.\\frac{d y}{d x}=\\frac{2 x}{8}=\\frac{x}{4}, \\frac{d y}{d x}\\right]_{x=4}=1$\nSlope of normal $=-\\frac{1}{\\frac{d y}{d x}}=-1$\nEuqation of normal at $x=4$ is $y-2=-1(x-4)$\n$\\Rightarrow y=-x+4+2=-x+6$\n$\\Rightarrow x+y=6$",
    "image": null
  },
